#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:875
msgid "Automatic X-Ray (all books)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:878
msgid ""
"Automatically build and maintain every book's X-Ray as you read (flowing "
"formats like EPUB only): a spoiler-free introduction first, then checkpoints "
"at chapter-sized steps, always keeping the next checkpoint ready ahead of "
"you; reaching it installs it instantly and the one after starts building. "
"Individual books can override this either way: X-Ray popup or Book Settings "
"→ Automatic X-Ray; a per-book On works even with this off, and a per-book "
"Off always wins.\n"
"\n"
"Spend guards: at most one background build per cooldown, WiFi only, and text-"
"extraction consent (or a trusted provider) required; background runs extract "
"book text and use API tokens without a per-request tap. Leave off if every "
"request should be explicit."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:900
msgid "Also Start X-Rays Automatically"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:903
msgid ""
"A sub-setting of Automatic X-Ray (all books), for books that have NO X-Ray "
"yet: allow automation to make the FIRST build (introduction + checkpoints to "
"your position; the first build asks how you want coverage, once per book). "
"With this off, \"all books\" automation only maintains X-Rays you started "
"yourself. Books with an existing non-incremental X-Ray (complete, AI-"
"knowledge, legacy) are never touched.\n"
"\n"
"Books switched to Automatic individually (per-book On) always build the "
"first one, regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:909
msgid "First Build for New Books"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:913
msgid "Ask each book"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:914
msgid "Catch up, then follow"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:915
msgid "Build all checkpoints"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:917
msgid ""
"How Automatic X-Ray handles its first build for a book. \"Ask each book\" "
"shows a one-time choice per book. \"Catch up, then follow\" quietly builds "
"checkpoints to your position and keeps one ahead. \"Build all checkpoints\" "
"offers the full checkpoint build with its cost confirmation. The ask "
"dialog's \"Always do this, for every book\" writes this setting too."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:922
msgid "Offer Automatic X-Ray for New Books"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:925
msgid ""
"When you open a book that has no X-Ray, ask once whether to turn on "
"Automatic X-Ray for it. Only asks when it could act right away (flowing "
"format, text-extraction consent in place). Declining turns the book's "
"Automatic X-Ray off, so it never asks again for that book."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:934
msgid "Cooldown (minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:941
msgid "Minimum time between background checkpoint builds (0 = no cooldown)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:947
msgid "Notify on Background Activity"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:950
msgid ""
"Show a brief notification when a background X-Ray update or create starts "
"and completes, and when a checkpoint is silently swapped in. Off = fully "
"silent (the X-Ray popup always shows the current coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:956
msgid "Checkpoints at Chapter Ends"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:959
msgid ""
"When building X-Ray checkpoints, place each checkpoint at the nearest "
"chapter end (within a few percent) instead of an exact percentage; "
"checkpoints then read as \"up to the end of a chapter\", and the versions "
"list shows the chapter names. Needs a table of contents. Checkpoint spacing "
"itself adapts to book length: about every 10% of a normal-length book, "
"larger steps for short ones."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:964
msgid "Categories for New X-Rays"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:966
msgid ""
"Which category groups a new X-Ray tracks by default: everything, or a "
"narrower pick like character tracking. Applies when an X-Ray is created or "
"rebuilt; individual books can pick their own categories in Book Settings."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:971
msgid "Shorter Update Requests"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:974
msgid ""
"When updating an X-Ray (manually or through checkpoints), send the model "
"only the most recent entries of the ever-growing event lists (timeline, "
"argument development) instead of the whole lists, which makes updates "
"noticeably cheaper on long books. The stored X-Ray always keeps all entries; "
"this only shortens what is sent. In rare cases the model may re-add an old "
"event it can no longer see."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:979
msgid "X-Ray Entry for Matching Selections"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:982
msgid ""
"When a tapped word or selected text exactly matches an X-Ray entity's name "
"or alias, open that X-Ray entry directly — skipping ahead of the dictionary "
"and the highlight menu (including any bypass actions you have set there). "
"Anything that doesn't match falls through to your normal dictionary/"
"highlight behavior. Only does anything for books that have an X-Ray. A very "
"long press at the end of a selection always shows the normal highlight menu."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:1000
msgid ""
"Discreetly underline words on the page that match an X-Ray entity's name or "
"alias, as you read (dotted gray, drawn shortly after the page settles; "
"entirely on-device). Tap a marked word to open its entry. Only active for "
"books that have an X-Ray. EPUB page mode only."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:1013
msgid "Tap Marked Words to Open"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:1016
msgid ""
"With passive marking on, a plain tap on a marked word opens its X-Ray entry, "
"like a link (real links in the text still win). Off = marks are visual only; "
"a long press still opens matching entries via \"X-Ray Entry for Matching "
"Selections\"."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:1032
msgid ""
"Let marking, matching selections and entity cards recognize entities that "
"first appear past your installed X-Ray coverage, using the checkpoint "
"already built ahead of you. Identification only: such names get short-dash "
"marks and a brief card, and the full entry stays behind a spoiler "
"confirmation. Off = the plugin only knows entities up to your installed "
"coverage."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:1045
msgid "Entity Card First"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:1048
msgid ""
"Exact entity hits (tapping a marked word, or selecting text that matches an "
"entity) open a compact card first: the name, category and role, and a one-"
"line identification, with the full entry a tap on the card away. The "
"identification may come from the newest built checkpoint, so newly appearing "
"names are known on sight — the full entry stays at your reading position, "
"behind a confirmation, while spoiler protection is on. Off = open the full "
"entry directly."
msgstr ""

